# Cursor Inline Diff Lens (`cursor-inline-diff-lens`)

Cursor IDE's signature developer experience is its high-density **Ghost Text & Inline Diff Lens**, where developers see exactly what lines will be added, replaced, or removed with color-coded clarity before execution.

This skill equips Antigravity CLI with Cursor-style inline diff previews, standardizing compact Unified Diff notation.

---

## 1. Unified Diff Preview Format

When proposing or verifying multi-line changes:

```diff
--- a/xrGame/weapon_ak74.cpp
+++ b/xrGame/weapon_ak74.cpp
@@ -212,5 +212,5 @@ void CWeaponAK74::FireTrace() {
-    u32 pOwner = (u32)H_Parent(); // Truncates 64-bit address on Linux!
+    uintptr_t pOwner = (uintptr_t)H_Parent();
     if (!pOwner) return;
```

---

## 2. Operating Directives

1. **Zero Surrounding Fluff:** Only show the modified line and 1–2 surrounding context lines. Never dump 50 lines of untouched code.
2. **Deterministic Line Coordinates:** Always specify exact line numbers (`@@ -start,count +start,count @@`).
3. **Ghost-Text Verification:** Compare proposed diffs against git status using `git diff -U2` to ensure surgical precision before committing.
